   "text": {
    "L1": "A circuit diagram uses standard symbols, so anyone can read the same circuit.",
    "L2": "A cell is shown by two unequal parallel lines. The longer thin line is positive.",
    "L3": "Two or more cells joined positive to negative make a battery.",
    "L4": "A bulb is a circle with a cross, and a switch is a gap in the line.",
    "L5": "When the switch is ON, it closes the gap and completes the circuit.",
    "L6": "When the switch is OFF, it opens the gap and breaks the circuit everywhere in one loop.",
    "L7": "The cell is the source of electricity. The switch only controls the path; it does not make or store electricity.",
    "L8": "A switch works before or after the bulb because any break stops the whole loop."
   },
